 "path": ".openclaw/tmp/continual_arc_grid_replication.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC observation: replicate a patterned cell of a divider grid

When a grid has uniform divider lines (e.g. a full row/column in a distinct color) splitting it into congruent regions, and one region contains a pattern while sibling regions are mostly background, replicate that pattern into the other regions without changing its orientation. Keep the divider lines intact. Verify regions have matching dimensions and preserve background cells in the copied tile.

Evidence: task-feaa278f demo used a 29x5 grid with two full horizontal separator rows; the nonempty 9-row band was repeated into all three bands. Test had a full horizontal and vertical separator, splitting into 6x6 quadrants; the populated top-right quadrant's 6x6 tile was copied to the other three quadrants. Submission was accepted. This is an observed task rule, not a universal ARC assumption; request a demo if unclear."
}
